From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:51:42 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Semantic completion on files that import modules

Completion on a file that imports modules keeps the semantic parser by default (index-only completion is an explicit opt-in), refreshes stale module dependencies against the request filesystem, waits for initial inputs and the resolved compile command on the first completion, reuses the preamble's actual build mode, and traces dependency validation separately from semantic execution.

* [clangd] Module support retains semantic completion by default

* Refresh stale module dependencies for semantic completion

* perf(clangd): completion trace separates dependency validation and semantic execution

* Fix initial module completion scheduling and resolved compile commands

* [clangd] Preserve preamble build mode for semantic completion

  Use the actual preamble mode when preparing completion instead of repeating module provider inventory. Retain late current-input and prerequisite validation before reusing any preamble or module file.
